    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15143#discussion_r4470592196\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Let's not rename functions at import time like this, <em>especially</em> when the rename is semantically meaningful!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637572289,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793811524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15143#discussion_r4470586358\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is an oddly specific test. If we want to unit-test the string parsing (and we probably should) then maybe just run through a series of test pairs (<code>\"0\" -&gt; Err, \"1s\" -&gt; Duration::from_secs(1), \"1ms\" -&gt; ...</code>)?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637572290,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793811524
